      "math_academy_id": "e-13201",
      "problem": "Given that $Y =\\{\\mu\\}$ and $Z =\\{1,2\\},$ find $\\left|\\mathcal{P}(\\mathcal{P}(Y\\times Z))\\right|.$",
      "worked_solution": "For any set $S,$ we have $\\left|\\mathcal{P}(S)\\right| = 2^{\\left| S \\right|}.$ Also, $|S \\times T| = |S| \\cdot |T|.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\left| Y \\right| = 1, \\qquad\n\\left| Z \\right| = 2.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(Y\\times Z)| & ={2}^{|Y\\times Z|} \\\\  & ={2}^{|Y|\\,\\cdot \\,|Z|} \\\\  & ={2}^{1\\cdot 2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(P(Y\\times Z))| & ={2}^{|P(Y\\times Z)|} \\\\  & ={2}^{4} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
